Records live here: one plans/records/<id>.md per entry from `researched` on,
and one per entry a migration touched, whatever its state.

This file exists so the directory is tracked from the first commit. Two
things point at it and would otherwise be describing something absent:
.markdownlint-cli2.yaml's `plans/records/**` ignore (owner ruling: the
archive is exempt from the style gate, because reformatting it would rewrite
the very text migrate-queue.py asserts moved across unchanged), and
tools/queue/render-queue-docs.py's record-heading checks.

Delete it once the directory holds real records.
